homelab-prometheus (0.10.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rules for DNS over IPv6 (post-cutover #64): DnsIPv6FrontendIdle (an
    edge busy on its IPv4 listener but silent on [::]:53 for 2 h) and
    ResolverIPv6Idle (ns03 answering nothing over IPv6 for 6 h while IPv4
    questions keep coming). Symptom-based: the monitoring host has no IPv6
    of its own to probe with.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Wed, 12 Nov 2026 09:40:00 -0600

homelab-prometheus (0.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Alertmanager (post-cutover #38): Depends on prometheus-alertmanager and
    configures it on this host, loopback only (127.0.0.1:9093, no cluster),
    from new ALERT_* keys in /etc/homelab/prometheus/config: one email
    receiver through the fleet's service mailbox (STARTTLS on 587 via the
    mail VIP, password in /etc/homelab/prometheus/alert-smtp.pw root:prometheus
    0640, TLS verified against ALERT_SMTP_SERVER_NAME). critical pages at once
    and repeats every 4 h, warning batches 5-10 min and repeats daily, a
    critical silences the host's warnings, resolved notices on. Plain-text
    subject/body templates. With ALERT_MAIL_TO empty or the password file
    missing an unconfigured Alertmanager (null receiver) is installed instead,
    loudly. prometheus.yml gains the alerting block; amtool is pointed at it.
  * New rules/fleet-basics.yml: HostDown, RootDiskFilling, MailQueueExpiring,
    DatabaseExporterDown, Watchdog (fires forever, routed nowhere: the proof
    the pipeline is alive).

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:20:00 -0600

